      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T05:00:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the request path, as you say the transport info is never used and this will always be empty. But this is fine, because that\u0027s not really the point – the point of this check here is the other path, the one that checks the factory is allowed to set these allowed UIDs.\n\nSo you are right that there isn\u0027t really a way for the wifi carrier service app to request a CBS network (on T or even on V for that matter). But there is still value in doing this because the factory path will still grant access to the correct process.\n\nIf you need a way for the service app to *request* the network, you\u0027ll first have to discuss with WiFi a way to tell the WiFi component about this in the request.",
